title The rebase that walks around the wall
prompt Continue the lap this seat claimed at its last close -- the pre-push conflict-marker placement booked as %731.
think Reds first outranks the lane, and the claim was mine, pushed, and unbuilt; leaving it open would invite a peer to build it twice.
think Before writing a line I asked why the card could ship markers at all when pre-commit rule nine already reads the same scan of the staged set, expecting to find the rule absent.
think The rule is present and correct, so the question became which commit it never saw -- and the answer was measured in a pen rather than reasoned: a pre-commit hook printing on every entry fired three times for three git commit calls and not once for the rebase that followed.
think That turned the whole lap from a guard into a placement, which is exactly the sentence the spine rule one room over already wrote for %681, so the second rule went into the same hook rather than into a second instrument.
think The narrowing was the one design choice: gate the push's own paths and REPORT a marker outside them, on the clause published_doubles already earns -- a gate that reds on what this lap cannot repair is a gate somebody turns off.
obs THE MECHANISM IS ONE SENTENCE PROVEN ON METAL: `git rebase --continue` commits without running `pre-commit`, on git 2.54.0. Case 12 of the new pen reproduces it end to end -- three commits, one conflicted rebase resolved with the marker left in, the hook's entry count read back, and the marker read out of the committed blob.
obs THE PEN FOUND A FAULT IN THE HOOK WHILE IT WAS BEING WRITTEN, and it is the leg worth keeping. The split between my markers and a peer's used `NR==FNR` against a keep-list that is EMPTY in exactly the peer case, and an empty first file leaves `NR==FNR` true for every line of the second -- so the negated form swallowed the whole hit list and the hook welcomed a peer's marker in silence, at exit 0, with its own control watching. Both splits are guarded now.
obs THE SPINE CONTROL RED THE MOMENT THE SECOND RULE LANDED, and that was the honest answer rather than a nuisance: its pen armed the hook and carried no marker scan, so every push in it refused. A pen that arms half a hook proves its rule against a wall no ship runs. It copies the marker scan now.
obs TWO MUTATIONS BITE. Flipping the publishes test drops six cases; restoring the unguarded awk drops exactly the peer case and nothing else, which is what makes that leg a measurement rather than a decoration.
obs WHAT IT DOES NOT REACH: a push made with --no-verify, already forbidden by git-signing and reachable by no guard in the tree.
obs THE HOT ROSTER READS 292 GUARDS, 286 GREEN, 4 RED, 2 GATED, `tree_moved=no`. My two are green by name -- `pre_push_spine` and `pre_push_marker`. NONE OF THE FOUR REDS IS MINE, and three of them already have a hand: `shim_reason` is patchouli's live claim by name, `fixture_depth` names `tools/fixtures/l/link_text_promise_scan.sh` and petrichor's live claim is that room, and `standing_equipment` is the aggregate of the others rather than a fault of its own. The fourth is `prose_register` at `law_over_field_target=10` against a ceiling of 9, pushed over by `.claude/rules/vocabulary-flaky.md` at 36 percent, seated by another ship at `20260915.183900` with its ceiling left where it stood. Reported rather than taken: a claim never touches a peer's in-flight work.
loom pre_push_marker cases_ok=14 cases_red=0 mutations_bitten=2 pen_seconds=10
loom pre_push_spine cases_ok=12 cases_red=0
loom conflict_marker files_scanned=18069 marker_lines=0 marked_files=0
obs THE SEND MET A PEER WHO HAD FOUND THE SAME THING. Copal booked `%732` -- the commit-time half, that `pre-commit` is not bypassed but NOT INVOKED by a rebase -- three minutes after my claim went up, read the claim, and deliberately did not build over it. Both rows stand; `%731` now points at `%732` for the mechanism rather than restating it.
obs THE LEDGER PIN ARRIVED 32 BYTES UNDER ITS 65,536 BOUND with six peer rows landed today, so my BOOKED clause was CONDENSED to fit rather than grown -- the pin stands exactly at its bound and the next lap to touch it owes a fold. Named on the card.
loom roster hot_guards=292 green=286 red=4 gated=2 seconds=4455 tree_moved=no
rota lap 4943, row 4 -- Earth, the row that breathes in; hand-advanced past row 3, read by this seat earlier today. Its cardinal page says a mark promises only what the work can keep, and the refusal this lap wrote keeps its promise by naming the file, the line, and the bypass that made it.
file tools/hooks/pre-push carries a second rule beside the spine one, narrowed to the push's own paths
file tools/fixtures/p/pre_push_marker_control.sh proves fourteen behaviors on real repositories, real pushes, and one real rebase
file tools/p/pre_push_marker_witness.rish gates the pen and the arming, and asserts the founding case by name
file tools/fixtures/p/pre_push_spine_control.sh arms the whole hook in its own pen rather than half of it
file construction/standing-equipment.kyri rosters pre_push_marker at tier lap
file construction/REDS.md books %731 as BOOKED with the mechanism and the fault the pen found
scope build the placement this seat claimed: ask the conflict-marker scan at the pre-push seam, prove it both ways, roster it
status GREEN before send -- pre_push_marker and pre_push_spine both green on metal, hot roster pass read after staging
recommend keep-going -- the moonshot lane is clear again; the two-lane question on the card still wants Keaton's word
